# Poker Programming Experiments

A collection of JavaScript experiments exploring poker-hand evaluation and interactive card selection.

The project includes:

- Representation of a standard 52-card deck
- Identification of poker hands, including straights, flushes, and full houses
- Comparison of hand rankings
- Interactive browser-based card selection
- Graphical output using Chart.js

## Demonstrations

- [Poker Hand Evaluator](https://jonathak.github.io/cards.html)
- [Card Selection Interface](https://jonathak.github.io/pear.html)
- [Three-Card Selector](https://jonathak.github.io/plum.html)

## Technology

JavaScript, HTML, CSS, and Chart.js.

## Status

Personal programming experiments. The code is exploratory and is not intended as a production poker application.
